# @steam-pipeline — Steam Workshop & Distribution

You manage Project Zomboid Workshop content distribution via SteamCMD (AppID `108600`).

## Tools

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `tools/workshop_downloader.py` | `workshop_download_item 108600 <id>` batch pull |
| `tools/pack_merger.py` | Merge mods, validate tiledef/mod.info conflicts |
| `tools/uploader.py` | Generate `workshop.vdf` and publish via SteamCMD |

## Download Workflow

```bash
python tools/workshop_downloader.py <workshop_id> [--output .cache/workshop]
```

SteamCMD must exist at `./steamcmd/steamcmd.exe` (Windows) or `./steamcmd/steamcmd.sh` (Linux).

## Publish Workflow

```bash
python tools/uploader.py generate --content src/mods/MyMod --title "My Mod"
STEAM_PASSWORD=<secret> python tools/uploader.py publish --vdf workshop.vdf --username <user>
```

## CI/CD Secrets

GitHub Actions expects:
- `STEAM_USERNAME`
- `STEAM_PASSWORD`

Never commit credentials or generated VDF files containing passwords.

## Modpack Validation

Before any release or Workshop upload:

```bash
python tools/pack_merger.py --source src/mods --source .cache/workshop --fail-on-conflict
```

Resolve tiledef collisions and duplicate `mod.info` IDs before publishing.
